# Laravel Microservices Specialist Rules

Curated patterns for the SAR2 Laravel microservices project (Student / Course / Enrollment services).
These rules complement `laravel-boost.mdc` with domain-specific patterns.

---

## 1. Inter-Service Testing with Http::fake() ⭐ MOST IMPACTFUL

**Always** use `Http::fake()` in enrollment-service tests to isolate from live student/course services.
Never let tests make real HTTP calls to other services — tests must pass without other services running.

```php
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Http;

public function test_can_create_enrollment(): void
{
    Http::fake([
        'localhost:8001/api/students/*' => Http::response([
            'id' => 1, 'full_name' => 'Alice Smith', 'email' => 'alice@example.com',
        ], 200),
        'localhost:8002/api/courses/*' => Http::response([
            'id' => 1, 'name' => 'Math 101', 'credits' => 3,
        ], 200),
    ]);

    $response = $this->postJson('/api/enrollments', [
        'student_id' => 1,
        'course_id'  => 1,
    ]);

    $response->assertStatus(201)
        ->assertJsonStructure(['id', 'student_id', 'course_id', 'enrolled_at']);
}

public function test_returns_422_when_student_service_down(): void
{
    Http::fake([
        'localhost:8001/api/students/*' => Http::response([], 404),
        'localhost:8002/api/courses/*'  => Http::response(['id' => 1, 'name' => 'Math 101'], 200),
    ]);

    $this->postJson('/api/enrollments', ['student_id' => 99, 'course_id' => 1])
        ->assertStatus(422);
}
```

Assert that the enrollment service actually called the other services:
```php
Http::assertSent(fn ($request) =>
    str_contains($request->url(), 'localhost:8001/api/students/1')
);
```

