## 4. Eloquent Query Scopes

Add named scopes to Eloquent models for reusable query constraints. Never inline complex queries in controllers.

```php
// In Enrollment model
public function scopeForStudent(Builder $query, int $studentId): void
{
    $query->where('student_id', $studentId);
}

public function scopeForCourse(Builder $query, int $courseId): void
{
    $query->where('course_id', $courseId);
}

public function scopeEnrolledAfter(Builder $query, string $date): void
{
    $query->where('enrolled_at', '>=', $date);
}

// Usage in controller
$enrollments = Enrollment::forStudent($studentId)->get();
```

