## 5. Model Observers for Cascade Cleanup

Use Observers to handle side effects (e.g., notifying enrollment-service when a student is deleted)
rather than putting logic in controllers.

```php
// app/Observers/StudentObserver.php
namespace App\Observers;

use App\Models\Student;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Http;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Log;

class StudentObserver
{
    public function deleted(Student $student): void
    {
        try {
            Http::delete("http://localhost:8003/api/enrollments/student/{$student->id}");
        } catch (\Exception $e) {
            // Enrollment service down — log but do not block the delete
            Log::warning("Could not cascade-delete enrollments for student {$student->id}: {$e->getMessage()}");
        }
    }
}

// Register in AppServiceProvider::boot()
Student::observe(StudentObserver::class);
```

