## 6. Eager Loading & N+1 Prevention

Never access relationships without eager loading. Always use `with()`.

```php
// ❌ Bad — N+1 in enrollment listing
$enrollments = Enrollment::all();
foreach ($enrollments as $e) {
    echo $e->student->full_name; // Each triggers a new query
}

// ✅ Good — eager load
$enrollments = Enrollment::with(['student', 'course'])->get();

// ✅ Good — withCount for aggregates
$courses = Course::withCount('enrollments')->get();
echo $course->enrollments_count;

// ✅ Good — chunking for large datasets (avoid memory exhaustion)
Enrollment::chunk(100, function ($chunk) {
    foreach ($chunk as $enrollment) {
        // process...
    }
});
```

