## 7. JSON Response Standards

Consistent response shapes across all three services:

```php
// Success list — 200
return response()->json($students, 200);

// Success single — 200
return response()->json($student, 200);

// Created — 201
return response()->json($student, 201);

// No content (delete) — 200 with message OR 204
return response()->json(['message' => 'Deleted successfully.'], 200);

// Validation error — handled automatically by Form Request (422)

// Not found — 404
return response()->json(['message' => 'Student not found.'], 404);

// Inter-service failure — 422
return response()->json(['message' => 'Student not found in Student Service.'], 422);
```

